481
00:27:36,364 --> 00:27:37,948
MISSED CALLS
SWEET JAE-YOON

482
00:27:38,115 --> 00:27:39,742
CALL FAILED
SWEET JAE-YOON

483
00:27:40,284 --> 00:27:44,245
[sobbing]

484
00:27:44,246 --> 00:27:46,832
[Paolo] Ah! We're completely surrounded.

485
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:49,126
Ah! Oh!

486
00:27:52,797 --> 00:27:54,131
- Oh, Paolo! Oh.
- Huh?

487
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:56,384
- Paolo, where's your gun?
- Gun?

488
00:27:57,009 --> 00:27:58,385
I... Elevator I think.

489
00:27:58,386 --> 00:28:00,304
- [comical music playing]
- [In-ho exclaims]

490
00:28:01,097 --> 00:28:03,765
{\an8}- [radio beeps]
- [Paolo] Oh, what the fuck is happening?

491
00:28:03,766 --> 00:28:06,018
- [radio static]
- What is all this?

492
00:28:06,602 --> 00:28:08,854
Uh, is it the Three Calamities?

493
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:12,566
- Ah, this is insane.
- Private Lee Jae-yoon here.

494
00:28:13,567 --> 00:28:15,027
Sergeant? Corporal?

495
00:28:15,653 --> 00:28:16,529
Is everyone okay?

496
00:28:18,239 --> 00:28:19,989
[on radio] <i>This is
Corporal Kwak Gye-young.</i>

497
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:21,575
<i>Soo-jeong and I are okay.</i>

498
00:28:22,701 --> 00:28:26,872
[Young-man on radio] <i>Uh, yeah.
Kyung-sik and I are also okay.</i>

499
00:28:27,832 --> 00:28:30,041
Ra In-Ho, Paolo and I are doing all right.

500
00:28:30,042 --> 00:28:31,710
[radio static whooshing]

501
00:28:33,254 --> 00:28:36,507
Any chance Arron Park is with you guys?

502
00:28:39,093 --> 00:28:41,429
Uh, Arron Park isn't currently with us...

503
00:28:42,471 --> 00:28:43,556
but he seems okay.

504
00:28:44,807 --> 00:28:47,351
[both exhale deeply]

505
00:28:48,394 --> 00:28:49,770
[Soo-jeong clears throat]

506
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:54,274
[both giggling awkwardly]

507
00:28:54,275 --> 00:28:56,651
- That's funny.
- Oh, Soo-jeong.

508
00:28:56,652 --> 00:28:59,612
I'll clean this up for you.
You can lie down and rest.

509
00:28:59,613 --> 00:29:01,573
[Gye-young chuckles]

510
00:29:01,574 --> 00:29:04,534
I don't want to.
Why the hell would I do that?

511
00:29:04,535 --> 00:29:06,619
Huh? What is wrong with you, bro?

512
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:09,790
Okay, I see the issue. [chuckles]

513
00:29:10,499 --> 00:29:13,835
Yeah. I think you're misunderstanding
what I'm trying to say here.

514
00:29:13,836 --> 00:29:15,463
Maybe you'd like to relax?

515
00:29:20,050 --> 00:29:21,385
That's not what I meant.

516
00:29:21,719 --> 00:29:23,304
All I was trying to do was...

517
00:29:23,846 --> 00:29:25,805
Usually, it's common courtesy to--

518
00:29:25,806 --> 00:29:29,058
You know what?
Just forget it. Okay? Yeah. Yeah.

519
00:29:29,059 --> 00:29:30,519
Just rest. Yeah, okay.

520
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:32,688
Huh.

521
00:29:33,439 --> 00:29:35,024
[Young-joo strains]

522
00:29:36,025 --> 00:29:38,027
[amusing music playing]

523
00:29:41,030 --> 00:29:43,491
[groaning]

524
00:29:52,041 --> 00:29:53,667
Employees pay for these?

525
00:29:54,502 --> 00:29:56,670
[sighs] Public enterprise welfare, my ass.

526
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:16,314
[gasps]

527
00:30:16,315 --> 00:30:18,359
[drum roll]

528
00:30:20,653 --> 00:30:21,779
Awesome.

529
00:30:22,363 --> 00:30:26,366
[whimpering] Oh, this really sucks.

530
00:30:26,367 --> 00:30:28,201
[radio static, beeping]

531
00:30:28,202 --> 00:30:30,245
[Young-man on radio]
<i>We don't have enough ammo</i>

532
00:30:30,246 --> 00:30:31,913
<i>to shoot our way through.</i>

533
00:30:31,914 --> 00:30:33,331
There's too many zombies.

534
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:35,625
[inhales, exhales]

535
00:30:35,626 --> 00:30:37,961
There's gotta be
a safe way for us to get out.

536
00:30:37,962 --> 00:30:38,879
<i>Any ideas?</i>

537
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:42,924
Do you guys think
we could blow up the zombies?

538
00:30:42,925 --> 00:30:45,677
We could throw a few grenades
and then run downstairs.

539
00:30:45,678 --> 00:30:46,679
That's impossible.

540
00:30:47,429 --> 00:30:51,308
An explosion of that magnitude would
attract the attention of all the zombies.

541
00:30:53,102 --> 00:30:54,228
[Jae-yoon sighs]

542
00:30:56,564 --> 00:30:57,690
Cancel that.

543
00:31:00,526 --> 00:31:01,609
[Soo-jeong sighs]

544
00:31:01,610 --> 00:31:04,238
We have to conserve these,
if that's all that we've got.

545
00:31:07,449 --> 00:31:09,033
- Hmm?
- All yours.

546
00:31:09,034 --> 00:31:10,494
Oh, thank you.

547
00:31:17,209 --> 00:31:19,295
{\an8}KWAK GYE-YOUNG
INSTAGRAM: GYE_TO_THE_YOUNG

548
00:31:20,254 --> 00:31:21,337
{\an8}Hey, what is this?

549
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:23,215
{\an8}Huh? Huh?

550
00:31:24,258 --> 00:31:25,091
{\an8}Oh.

551
00:31:25,092 --> 00:31:27,177
[soft music playing]

552
00:31:32,683 --> 00:31:36,270
f somehow we survive this,
I'd like to go on a date with you.

553
00:31:36,979 --> 00:31:41,733
The thing is, you know,
I don't think it's really the time

554
00:31:41,734 --> 00:31:43,110
for this kind of shit.

555
00:31:43,694 --> 00:31:47,405
Yes. I know that,
but here's the thing, Soo-jeong.

556
00:31:47,406 --> 00:31:50,659
[sighs] Uh, all of my entire life

557
00:31:51,285 --> 00:31:54,245
I've always just sort of sat back
and gone with the flow.

558
00:31:54,246 --> 00:31:56,332
Acting that way will get me killed now.

559
00:31:58,375 --> 00:32:01,462
And I've realized
that I need a reason to live.

560
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:04,172
You make me want to live another day.

561
00:32:04,173 --> 00:32:06,007
That's a brand new feeling for me.

562
00:32:06,008 --> 00:32:09,011
What I'm trying to say is, you are...

563
00:32:12,473 --> 00:32:14,642
the only motivation I need
to get through this.

564
00:32:25,277 --> 00:32:27,279
Sure, I guess so.

565
00:32:27,905 --> 00:32:30,949
You have to take me to a nice restaurant.

566
00:32:31,617 --> 00:32:33,369
- You got it?
- [chuckles]

567
00:32:34,536 --> 00:32:35,745
Well, it's a date, then.

568
00:32:35,746 --> 00:32:37,664
[hesitates] Really? Okay.

569
00:32:37,665 --> 00:32:39,791
Oh, Soo-jeong, seriously?

570
00:32:39,792 --> 00:32:43,295
Oh. [hesitates]
Now the only option is survival.

571
00:32:43,921 --> 00:32:46,256
- [chuckles]
- Oh, my God! [laughs]

572
00:32:48,550 --> 00:32:49,551
Whatever.

573
00:32:52,763 --> 00:32:53,764
[grunts]

574
00:32:57,768 --> 00:32:58,769
What?

575
00:33:03,857 --> 00:33:04,692
Okay.

576
00:33:07,778 --> 00:33:10,322
[sighs] Does this thing even work?

577
00:33:11,115 --> 00:33:12,991
DEFECTIVE

578
00:33:13,409 --> 00:33:15,285
When it rains, it pours, doesn't it?

579
00:33:16,745 --> 00:33:18,122
- [woman] <i>Young-joo.</i>
- [gasps]

580
00:33:31,051 --> 00:33:34,345
Tch. Look at me putting my degree to work.

581
00:33:34,346 --> 00:33:36,890
I guess mechanical engineering
is saving my life.

582
00:33:38,016 --> 00:33:40,017
[woman] <i>Young-joo.</i>

583
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:42,311
Huh? What?

584
00:33:42,312 --> 00:33:44,273
Will you give it a rest already? Ugh!

585
00:33:46,150 --> 00:33:47,401
[sighs]

586
00:33:48,110 --> 00:33:49,111
- [whirrs]
- [gasps]

587
00:33:49,611 --> 00:33:52,990
- [whirring]
- [chuckles]

588
00:33:57,453 --> 00:33:58,287
Hi-ya!

589
00:34:13,469 --> 00:34:14,302
[chuckles]

590
00:34:14,303 --> 00:34:16,596
MY NAME IS KANG YOUNG-JOO,
AND I'M BORROWING SOME EQUIPMENT

591
00:34:16,597 --> 00:34:18,055
P.S. I HAD THE SOJU, NOODLES, AND CHIPS

592
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:20,142
[snarling]

593
00:34:26,565 --> 00:34:28,942
[Jae-yoon sighs]

594
00:34:30,277 --> 00:34:32,403
I don't think it's safe to go outside yet.

595
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:33,989
- [sighs] Huh?
- [Jae-yoon] What?

596
00:34:50,339 --> 00:34:52,216
- [In-ho] I found it.
- [Jae-yoon] What?

597
00:34:54,051 --> 00:34:55,635
- Hey, Lee-Jae-yoon!
- What is it?

598
00:34:55,636 --> 00:34:57,970
- I think we can use the vents to get out.
- [bell dings]

599
00:34:57,971 --> 00:35:01,766
- Wait. [exclaims] Why's he outside? Wait.
- [chuckling]

600
00:35:01,767 --> 00:35:03,351
Arron Park.

601
00:35:03,352 --> 00:35:05,311
- Hold up, I'll get the door.
- [Arron] <i>No, no.</i>

602
00:35:05,312 --> 00:35:07,397
[snarling]

603
00:35:08,190 --> 00:35:11,192
- [Jae-yoon] Huh?
<i>- The zombies don't bite me anymore.</i>

604
00:35:11,193 --> 00:35:14,904
<i>Just don't put yourself in danger
by opening up the door.</i>

605
00:35:14,905 --> 00:35:17,031
They don't bite. But why?

606
00:35:17,032 --> 00:35:18,992
<i>Why? Great question.</i>

607
00:35:21,036 --> 00:35:23,914
There must be a reason why
Arron Park isn't changing.

608
00:35:24,915 --> 00:35:25,833
<i>Anyway...</i>

609
00:35:26,458 --> 00:35:28,668
<i>You should know
that there's a way to get downstairs</i>

610
00:35:28,669 --> 00:35:31,170
<i>without having to use
the hallways or elevators.</i>

611
00:35:31,171 --> 00:35:33,089
Wait, really? Where do we go?

612
00:35:33,090 --> 00:35:35,133
<i>See that vent in the middle of the room?</i>

613
00:35:36,468 --> 00:35:37,803
<i>You can use it to escape.</i>

614
00:35:38,512 --> 00:35:40,472
<i>The vent has a way out for all of you.</i>

615
00:35:42,307 --> 00:35:45,978
[chuckles] <i>What do you think?
An excellent idea, right?</i>

616
00:35:46,520 --> 00:35:49,690
That is exactly what I was gonna say.

617
00:35:51,817 --> 00:35:53,568
This is Private Lee Jae-yoon.

618
00:35:53,569 --> 00:35:56,404
Sergeant Kim Young-man.
Corporal Kwak Gye-young, can you read me?

619
00:35:56,405 --> 00:35:58,323
Corporal Kwak Gye-young, awaiting orders.

620
00:36:00,242 --> 00:36:01,243
I'm here too.

621
00:36:02,327 --> 00:36:03,828
[Jae-yoon] <i>Everyone, pay attention.</i>

622
00:36:03,829 --> 00:36:07,081
<i>I'll go over the escape plan
that Arron Park and I put together.</i>

623
00:36:07,082 --> 00:36:10,167
All of your rooms should have a vent
right in the center of the ceiling.

624
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:12,044
<i>You'll first need to open the ventilator.</i>

625
00:36:12,045 --> 00:36:15,006
<i>You'll then need to widen
the ventilation entrance to fit through.</i>

626
00:36:15,007 --> 00:36:17,092
[thudding]

627
00:36:19,678 --> 00:36:22,263
[Jae-yoon] Use your rifles
or anything strong enough

628
00:36:22,264 --> 00:36:23,724
to start breaking down the wall.

629
00:36:24,391 --> 00:36:26,183
Although the vents should be empty,

630
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:29,437
we've seen hordes of zombies
every single step of the way.

631
00:36:29,438 --> 00:36:32,023
<i>So make sure to always be on the look.</i>

632
00:36:32,024 --> 00:36:33,858
<i>Once inside the ventilation system,</i>

633
00:36:33,859 --> 00:36:36,444
<i>you'll have to navigate it
and reach the main vent.</i>

634
00:36:36,445 --> 00:36:39,698
<i>From there, we'll have a direct way out
via the access ladders.</i>

635
00:36:40,699 --> 00:36:43,702
<i>Given the situation in the hallway,
I think this is our best option.</i>

636
00:36:44,536 --> 00:36:48,040
Okay, so we'll enter the vent
in exactly 30 minutes.

637
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:51,627
[Gye-young] <i>Okay.
Working on widening the entrance.</i>

638
00:36:54,338 --> 00:36:56,340
[thudding]

639
00:37:01,845 --> 00:37:03,846
[Arron] Whoa, whoa, there. [sighs]

640
00:37:03,847 --> 00:37:06,349
[snarling]

641
00:37:06,350 --> 00:37:08,435
Uh... Excuse me.

642
00:37:09,645 --> 00:37:11,396
Oh, oh, oh.

643
00:37:28,455 --> 00:37:30,331
Mrs. Kim shame on you.

644
00:37:30,332 --> 00:37:33,126
How many times did I ask you
not to drink at work, huh?

645
00:37:38,048 --> 00:37:39,049
[sighs]

646
00:37:40,175 --> 00:37:42,803
Three stashed bottles. Jeez, lady.
[clears throat]

647
00:37:47,140 --> 00:37:48,141
[gulping]

648
00:37:53,063 --> 00:37:53,897
Ah!

649
00:38:15,377 --> 00:38:17,712
[Gye-young] <i>We just have
to follow the vents, right?</i>

650
00:38:17,713 --> 00:38:19,588
<i>How will we know which way to go?</i>

651
00:38:19,589 --> 00:38:22,217
[Jae-yoon] <i>Arron Park
will be guiding us through the vents.</i>

652
00:38:23,176 --> 00:38:25,469
<i>He supervised
the ventilation system's construction</i>

653
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:27,096
<i>and knows the layout by heart.</i>

654
00:38:27,097 --> 00:38:31,142
<i>He'll mark arrows to show the right path
we must take to reach the main vent.</i>

655
00:38:31,143 --> 00:38:33,770
<i>All our team needs to do
is follow the arrows.</i>

656
00:38:39,026 --> 00:38:39,943
That's the plan.

657
00:38:40,485 --> 00:38:42,029
We must be quick and quiet.

658
00:38:45,741 --> 00:38:48,409
Sergeant Kim Young-man,
Corporal Kwak Gye-young,

659
00:38:48,410 --> 00:38:49,578
awaiting your orders.

660
00:38:50,370 --> 00:38:52,121
Yes. We're all set here.

661
00:38:52,122 --> 00:38:54,373
Corporal Kwak Gye-young.
We're ready to go.

662
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:56,083
Good luck to everyone.

663
00:38:56,084 --> 00:38:57,669
See you all on the other side!

664
00:38:59,504 --> 00:39:00,671
How was that?

665
00:39:00,672 --> 00:39:03,382
Yeah. Gye-young is right, you guys.

666
00:39:03,383 --> 00:39:04,926
Everyone, make it out alive.

667
00:39:05,469 --> 00:39:06,386
That's an order.

668
00:39:07,304 --> 00:39:09,388
Directly from your squad commander.

669
00:39:09,389 --> 00:39:12,017
<i>- Yes, sir!
- Sir, yes, sir.</i>

670
00:39:12,809 --> 00:39:14,810
- Dumb asses.
- All squad members,

671
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:17,022
are now clear to begin their escape route.

672
00:39:22,152 --> 00:39:24,362
[In-ho grunting]

673
00:39:26,448 --> 00:39:28,450
Paolo, take my hand. Grab it.

674
00:39:38,335 --> 00:39:39,544
[Soo-jeong] Be careful.

675
00:39:40,253 --> 00:39:42,672
[grunting] Are you worried about me?

676
00:39:43,590 --> 00:39:45,175
[Soo-jeong] Shut up and climb!

677
00:39:46,676 --> 00:39:48,678
[grunting]

678
00:39:51,723 --> 00:39:53,809
Hey, you see the arrows?

679
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,311
Fucking hell.

680
00:39:58,188 --> 00:40:00,565
Kyung-sik! Wait for me.

681
00:40:03,819 --> 00:40:06,070
Ah, shit. [pants]

682
00:40:06,071 --> 00:40:08,448
[coughing]

683
00:40:13,912 --> 00:40:16,122
[Jae-yoon] Turn left. Turn left.

684
00:40:16,123 --> 00:40:18,208
[panting]

685
00:40:30,387 --> 00:40:31,388
Let's do this.

686
00:40:34,975 --> 00:40:36,977
[whirring]

687
00:40:39,563 --> 00:40:40,564
Okay.

688
00:40:47,487 --> 00:40:49,489
[snarling]

689
00:41:00,292 --> 00:41:02,294
[whirring]

690
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:11,469
[screaming]

691
00:41:26,318 --> 00:41:28,320
[screaming]

692
00:41:43,460 --> 00:41:44,294
Shit!

693
00:41:46,213 --> 00:41:47,379
[snarling]

694
00:41:47,380 --> 00:41:48,298
[screams]

695
00:41:57,766 --> 00:41:59,768
[panting]

696
00:42:03,521 --> 00:42:04,356
Hold on.

697
00:42:05,148 --> 00:42:06,358
All the arrows are gone.

698
00:42:08,401 --> 00:42:09,402
[Arron] What's up?

699
00:42:10,278 --> 00:42:12,821
[laughs] You actually made it.

700
00:42:12,822 --> 00:42:14,032
Are you okay, Paolo?

701
00:42:15,158 --> 00:42:16,076
No.

702
00:42:17,118 --> 00:42:19,453
I'm fine, Arron.
Let's just keep going, okay?

703
00:42:19,454 --> 00:42:20,746
God, I'm so hot.

704
00:42:20,747 --> 00:42:23,291
Hey, so, how far away are we?

705
00:42:24,334 --> 00:42:25,709
Almost there.

706
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:28,046
We're five minutes away,
so come on, let's go.

707
00:42:28,713 --> 00:42:30,340
Okay, let's go.

708
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:33,551
[grunting, panting]

709
00:42:36,471 --> 00:42:38,014
[Jae-yoon] Go, go, go. Go, go.

710
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:48,441
Where the fuck are the arrows?

711
00:42:49,401 --> 00:42:51,736
[strains]

712
00:42:53,613 --> 00:42:55,990
Hey, wait. Soo-jeong. Soo-jeong.

713
00:42:55,991 --> 00:42:57,866
- Huh?
- You're, um...

714
00:42:57,867 --> 00:42:59,868
You're tensing up your body.

715
00:42:59,869 --> 00:43:02,371
You'll get tired quicker
and won't advance much.

716
00:43:02,372 --> 00:43:04,123
What you need to do is relax your body

717
00:43:04,124 --> 00:43:06,125
and use both your forearms

718
00:43:06,126 --> 00:43:08,961
to push and you gradually move forward.

719
00:43:08,962 --> 00:43:10,422
[grunts] Like this.

720
00:43:11,298 --> 00:43:12,132
Oh.

721
00:43:13,300 --> 00:43:15,635
Like this? Oh!

722
00:43:16,219 --> 00:43:17,554
It's way easier like this.

723
00:43:19,806 --> 00:43:20,807
Right?

724
00:43:21,391 --> 00:43:23,393
Like this. Like this.

725
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:25,769
Like this.

726
00:43:25,770 --> 00:43:27,313
I don't really have many talents,

727
00:43:27,314 --> 00:43:29,732
but I did win first place in boot camp
for crawling.

728
00:43:29,733 --> 00:43:31,400
[Soo-jeong] Jesus Christ. [chuckles]

729
00:43:31,401 --> 00:43:33,569
[Gye-young] Not like that.
Relax your lower body.

730
00:43:33,570 --> 00:43:35,238
- Like this?
- [Gye-young] Like this.

